  "description": "The Bufflehead is a small diving duck with a rounded head and a buoyant appearance on the water. Males have striking black-and-white plumage, with green and purple iridescence visible on the head in good light. Females are gray-brown with a small white cheek patch. These ducks dive repeatedly to feed on aquatic invertebrates, often disappearing abruptly and resurfacing nearby. They spend winter on sheltered bays, lakes, and ponds, then breed in northern forests, where they use tree cavities, particularly old woodpecker holes, as nest sites.",
